# T21: without this, actions/checkout@v4 on windows-2022 honors that
# runner's global core.autocrlf=true and rewrites every text file's line
# endings to CRLF on checkout. Every generated file this repo's `gen:*`
# scripts write (scripts/gen-errors.js and friends) is written with LF
# endings regardless of host OS (plain Node fs.writeFileSync, no platform
# newline translation), so `npm run gen:check` compares that LF output
# against a CRLF-converted working-tree file and reports every generated
# file as "stale" -- discovered on windows-2022 in T21's build-windows job.
# `eol=lf` pins checked-out line endings to LF on every platform, overriding
# the runner's core.autocrlf; `text=auto` still lets git auto-detect binary
# files (so this rule is a no-op for them) while normalizing everything else.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary marks for the fixtures most likely to trip git's
# binary-detection heuristic if their content ever starts with mostly-ASCII
# bytes (TIFF/DNG headers can): never let these round-trip through any
# newline conversion.
*.dng binary
*.DNG binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.node binary
